{"event": "tool", "name": "finish", "args": {"summary": "**Question:** Total revenue by region for Electronics.\n\n**Result (from 12 of 13 Electronics rows):**\n| Region | Revenue |\n|--------|---------|\n| South  | $10,540 |\n| East   | $7,580  |\n| North  | $3,750  |\n| West   | $1,800  |\n\n**Data quality issues found and fixed:**\n- **Region label variants** (6 rows): Labels like \" South\", \"North \", \"east\", \"north\", \"west\" were normalized to the canonical \"South\", \"North\", \"East\", \"West\" using normalize_labels. This affected Electronics rows 11 and 17.\n\n**Issues found but not affecting the Electronics question:**\n- **Negative quantities** (rows 5, 14, 65): All are non-Electronics (Furniture, Office Supplies, Furniture). Not fixed since they don't impact this question.\n- **Revenue \u2260 Quantity \u00d7 Price** (rows 10, 19, 61): All non-Electronics (Accessories, Office Supplies, Office Supplies). Not fixed for this question.\n- **Invalid dates** (rows 48, 50, 64): Not relevant to this question.\n- **Missing Region** (rows 36, 40, 49): Row 36 is an Electronics order (Laptop, Revenue $5,400) with a missing Region. Since the rules file does not specify what the Region should be, I did not fill it. This row is excluded from the region breakdown, which is why only 12 of 13 Electronics rows are reflected in the totals above. The $5,400 from this row is not attributed to any region."}, "ok": true, "output": {"finished": true}, "t": 159.0}
